## What was installed

| Component | Version | Location |
|---|---|---|
| STP (solver) | 2.3.4 + MiniSat | `/usr/local/lib/libstp.so.2.3`, `STPConfig.cmake` in `/usr/local/lib/cmake/STP` |
| KLEE | 3.4-pre, `klee`/`kleaver`/`klee-stats`/`ktest-gen` | `/usr/local/bin` |
| Headers | `klee/klee.h`, `stp/c_interface.h` | `/usr/local/include` |
| Runtime bitcode | `libkleeRuntime*.bca` (KDAlloc default) | `/usr/local/lib/klee/runtime` |

Built from source against the pre-installed **LLVM 16** (the binary links `libLLVM-16.so.1`), with `ENABLE_SOLVER_STP=ON` — STP is the default `--solver-backend` — and **no uClibc** (`KLEE_UCLIBC_PATH` empty, so no `klee-uclibc.bca` is installed).

Two things worth flagging about this machine (aarch64, not x86):

- **POSIX runtime is disabled.** `runtime/POSIX/fd.c` uses `__NR_open`, `__NR_stat`, `__NR_access`, … which do not exist on arm64, so `ENABLE_POSIX_RUNTIME=ON` fails to compile. KLEE itself, the STP solver, and kernel/KDAlloc all work normally; only the `--posix-runtime` flag is unavailable.
- **No uClibc was wanted, so libc-backed programs** get KLEE's special-function handling for `assert` (`__assert_fail` is a KLEE special function — verified working) and warnings for unmodelled externals like `printf`.

## ~/.bashrc

Ubuntu's default `.bashrc` opens with `[ -z "$PS1" ] && return`, which would have skipped any appended exports when a test does `source ~/.bashrc` non-interactively. The KLEE block is therefore inserted **above** that guard (backup at `/root/.bashrc.bak-klee`), and it is idempotent:

```
CPATH=/usr/local/include:/usr/local/include/klee
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/usr/local/lib
```

`/usr/local/include` makes `#include <klee/klee.h>` resolve; `/usr/local/include/klee` is added too so a bare `#include <klee.h>` works. A matching `/etc/profile.d/klee.sh` covers login shells. `libstp` is also on the loader path via `/etc/ld.so.conf.d/local.conf` + `ldconfig`, so `klee` runs even with an empty environment.

## Verification

`verify_klee.sh` (committed at the repo root) sources `~/.bashrc` in a clean `env -i` shell exactly as the tests will, and checks: `klee` on PATH, CPATH contents, LLVM-16 build, STP backend, absence of any `klee-uclibc` archive, compiling `<klee/klee.h>` with **no `-I` flag**, a real symbolic run reaching an assertion violation, and header resolution from the CPATH entries:

